[i][b]My horse looks like a meatball ![/b][/i]
See the red text on black background in the Workshop page description.

[i][b]Does the mod work for MP ?[/b][/i]
Currently yes BUT riding is disabled for it until we make it work.

[i][b]I can't find horses on my map[/b][/i]
It might be that you created the save without restarting your game first with the mod active, which will make the horse ranch zones not spawn on world creation. 
This is a vanilla problem, and a fix you can do is to delete all apop files and the map_zone.bin file from the save, start the game with the mod enabled and then load the save. [b]This will delete all your animals and animal zones[/b]

[i][b]Is it safe to use on an old save ?[/b][/i]
Yes BUT horses will not be spawned in the world when you do that. You need to manually spawn them from debug mode. Alternatively, you can do the fix from the answer of the question above.
The reason is that the animal zones that they are defined to spawn in are only created when making a new save. This means there will be no horse ranch zones on the map so no naturally spawned horses.

[i][b]Can I shoot from horse back, or when will it be added ?[/b][/i]
You can't, and we'd like to add it, but it's very complicated to do so. Be very patient.

[i][b]Where do the horses spawn ?[/b][/i]
They spawn in ranches, some barns and fields, as well as some places that have different farm animals. 
[spoiler]Echo Creek is the place with the most amount of horses due to its ranches, barns and fields.[/spoiler]
[spoiler]In Louisville, there are 2 places where they spawn: the [url=https://b42map.com/?12224x2758]Horsetracks[/url] and in the [url=https://b42map.com/?13043x2827]Central Park Stables[/url][/spoiler]

[i][b]What's the load order for the mod ?[/b][/i]
Load order doesn't matter in general for mods.

[i][b]How can I stop my horse from wandering away ?[/b][/i]
You can tie your horse with a rope to a tree, like vanilla animals.

[i][b]What items can I attach on my horse ?[/b][/i]
Currently, you can attach on the horse:
- saddles
- saddlebags
- reins
- tents
- sleeping bags
We also have an API for modders to add their own equipment.

[i][b]Where can I find equipment for my horse ?[/b][/i]
You can craft saddles, saddlebags and reins or find them in:
- Farms/Barns (where farm/barn tools spawns)
- Camping equipment (like military surplus store, storage units etc.)
- The old western town (coalfield)
- The racetrack in LV
- Hunting lockers (like in hunting lodges)
- Sports stores
- Animal/Pet stores
- Survival gear spawns

[i][b]Do you plan on adding horse carts/wagons ?[/b][/i]
We didn't wait for the release of the mod to come to think about it, and while it'd be amazing to see, it wouldn't be that easy to implement. Horses are not vehicles, they are animals, and as such the systems in place to have vehicles tracking other vehicles cannot be used when it comes to horses. As such, don't expect this in a near update, but who knows, we might figure something out, and we kind of already have one or two ideas on how to possibly implement that.